Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:47:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix(packageinstaller): locate the installer's cloud-check
 skip by structure only

The old rule needed a "R.string.start_install" method and a six-argument
(Context, ?, int, ApkInfo, HashMap, Continuation) cloud-check method. Neither
exists in current installers (9.9.9.9.9 / 5.5.5.0.0), so initDexKit threw and
the whole rule - including the install_btn anchor that still matched - was
dropped.

Rebuild the rule from two semantic anchors: the method that uses "install_btn"
plus the constant 16, and, inside the same class, the same-prototype void method
that this button method itself calls (the direct-install call its allowed branch
makes). Hook the button method, invoke the direct-install method and null the
result, so the button is never rewritten to "continue update" and the risk
dialog listener is never bound. Any missing anchor returns false: the rule is
skipped and the installer keeps its stock behaviour instead of crashing.

Verified against both attached installers: t2.r#a2(q2.l) is the anchor and its
allowed branch calls t2.r#f2(q2.l) (u2(...,16,null); F1()); the old
start_install/6-arg anchors are absent in both.
